<h2>Highlights</h2>
<ul>
<li><a href="#benchmarks">63% fewer tokens</a> than Codex CLI on the same model, at the
same success rate.</li>
<li><a href="docs/auto-reasoning-effort.md"><strong>Auto reasoning effort</strong></a> — each message
and tool step gets the effort it needs, judged in about 0.1 s by a 150 MB
model that runs locally on the CPU. On by default.</li>
<li>Use the <strong>Claude, ChatGPT, Grok, or Muse Code</strong> subscription you already have, API
keys, or local models on your own GPU.</li>
<li>Mix models by role and scale from <strong>Solo to Swarm</strong> — a strong model leads
while cheaper ones search, edit, and review in parallel. Switch the workflow
or mode mid-conversation, and set fallback models for usage limits.</li>
<li><strong>Bots and rooms</strong> — your own bots with their own models, tools, and
permissions, group rooms where they talk together, and a representative bot
that sits above the composer on your desktop.</li>
<li>A full workspace: editor, terminals, Git and GitHub, code graph, and
language servers, with themes and photo skins.</li>
<li>Keeps working on its own with <strong>Goals, schedules, and webhooks</strong> — and
continues from your phone, end-to-end encrypted.</li>
<li>Goes beyond code with <strong>browser and desktop control</strong>, Office and PDF
documents, and image and video generation.</li>
<li>Runs on Windows, macOS, and Linux. No config files.</li>
</ul>
